# Packages removed from each desktop's rootfs before squashfs (system stage 5):
# `rpm -e --nodeps --noscripts` from the builder, then dnf's autoremove takes
# out what only they (or nothing) needed. build.sh's library guard fails the
# build if a library something left in the image links went with them.
#
# One rpm name per line; # comments and blank lines are ignored.
#   - Shell globs are allowed.
#   - A line starting with ! keeps the packages it matches.
#   - Names/globs that match nothing installed are ignored.
# Files of packages that must stay: remove-files.list.

# The package manager's runtime: the image is never changed in place. (The
# builder's dnf installed everything; dnf itself never entered the rootfs.)
rpm
rpm-plugin-*
rpm-sequoia*

# systemd-boot: the bootloader is a release file (stage 9 takes it from the
# base); nothing in the running system installs or updates it.
systemd-boot-unsigned

# Pulled in by NVIDIA's packages: grubby (their scriptlet adds kernel arguments
# to GRUB entries; larch boots systemd-boot with its own entries) and the
# nvidia-settings GUI (X11-only on Wayland).
grubby
grub2-*
os-prober
nvidia-settings*

# Initramfs generators pulled in by the kernel: every larch initramfs is
# assembled by hand (shared/build-lib.sh).
dracut*

# No privilege escalation on the immutable OS.
sudo
